# Validate a dotfiles branch on a clean macOS image.
#
# Nothing is mounted from the host on purpose: the whole point is that the
# guest clones from GitHub the way a fresh machine would, so a step that only
# works because of state already on this laptop fails here instead of on the
# next new machine.

tart clone ghcr.io/cirruslabs/macos-tahoe-base:latest tahoe-validate
tart set tahoe-validate --cpu 6 --memory 12288 --disk-size 90
tart run --no-graphics tahoe-validate &

# The image logs you in as admin/admin and that cannot be changed at clone
# time - `tart clone` copies a disk, it never runs Setup Assistant. Only
# `tart create --from-ipsw latest` gives a different primary user, and that
# means clicking through Setup Assistant with no guest agent and no ssh.
# Add the account instead; admin stays as the escape hatch.
#
# darwinConfigurations declare a user but do NOT create one: nix-darwin gates
# its whole user activation on `users.knownUsers != []`, and this repo sets
# knownUsers nowhere. The name is load-bearing - shesfast.nix and
# profiles/home.nix both hardcode /Users/alyssa.
tart exec tahoe-validate sudo sysadminctl -addUser alyssa \
  -fullName "Alyssa Evans" -password validate \
  -home /Users/alyssa -shell /bin/zsh -admin
tart exec tahoe-validate sudo createhomedir -c -u alyssa
#   Runnable: just -g tart-user tahoe-validate

# No ssh needed for any of this - the guest agent ships in the image and the
# account has passwordless sudo. See the community/tart/exec sheet.
tart exec -it tahoe-validate sudo -u alyssa -i zsh
#   or, for a long session:  ssh alyssa@$(tart ip tahoe-validate)

# inside the guest, either path:
#   Nix path      -> README, "macOS setup (Darwin)"
#   no-Nix path   -> curl -fsSL .../tools/mise/bootstrap.sh | sh
#                    then: mise run gh-login && mise run identity

# Three levels of validation, and only the last one needs the alyssa account:
#   evaluate  ./.github/scripts/eval-configurations.sh    # what CI does
#   build     nix build .#darwinConfigurations.shesfast.system
#   activate  darwin-rebuild switch --flake .#shesfast    <- needs the user
# Only `activate` catches what this repo keeps getting bitten by, which is the
# whole reason the VM exists (CLAUDE.md, Testing).

# Three things that do NOT block a run here, each checked rather than assumed:
#   - Homebrew absent is a SKIP, not an abort. nix-darwin prints a red
#     "Homebrew is not installed, skipping..." and carries on
#     (modules/homebrew.nix), so the whole Nix half validates without
#     downloading a single cask. Skip the README's `brew trust` step too.
#   - A missing age identity is non-fatal: agenix-activation.nix warns per
#     secret and returns 0. No need to carry personal-key.txt into the VM.
#   - agentSkills.liveCheckout defaults to null, so skills deploy from the
#     store and nothing assumes a checkout at ~/dotfiles. Clone anywhere.

tart stop tahoe-validate && tart delete tahoe-validate

# Why tahoe and not golden-gate, on a macOS 15 host: it is the image's DISK
# FORMAT that matters, not the guest's OS version. Golden Gate is published as
# asif, which needs a macOS 26 host, so `tart run` fails with
#
#   Error: Disk format 'asif' is not supported on this system.
#
# and it fails *after* the 30 GiB pull and after `tart set` succeeds, so there
# is no early signal. Tahoe is macOS 26 too and boots here fine because it is
# published raw - verified first-hand 2026-09-21, a macOS 26.6.2 (25G83) guest
# running on a macOS 15.7.4 host, so guest-newer-than-host was never the
# problem. Check the label before pulling:
# `just -g tart-image-format <name>`, or the community/tart/image sheet.

# Runnable: just -g tart-new tahoe-validate tahoe
